    "body": "Both causes are now covered, in the plugin repo — mirrored there as ix-codex-plugin#22, because GitHub closing keywords do not work across repositories and this issue would otherwise never auto-close.\n\n| cause | fix |\n|---|---|\n| `/bin/sh -lc` in all five `hooks.json` commands | ix-codex-plugin#20 |\n| `subprocess` not consulting `PATHEXT` for `ix.CMD` | ix-codex-plugin#19 |\n\nWorth being explicit that **neither alone is enough**: #19's fix lives inside `common.py`, and until #20 lands the hook process never starts, so that code never runs. #19's own description scopes it to \"the half that breaks the CLI\" — it is the half that is unreachable without the other.\n\nLeaving this open. Neither PR has been run on real Windows; both were written and tested on Linux, where the changed paths are no-ops or unit-tested in isolation. @tept-creator — a confirmation from a real Windows box after both merge is what should close this.",
